			<div class="content" id="post-content-2364971">
									

<p>That makes the three of us then. Huh.</p>
<p>Anyway, I wrote this literally overnight without bothering to consult any sources or my own memory, so that explains the platform naming error. As for &quot;metro system&quot;, I'm using what seems to be an international term, as opposed to a local term that warrants an explanation&#8230; no harm changing to MRT and providing a footnote, but I also don't see any problem in not changing.</p>
<p>And it's completely obvious it's Dhoby Ghaut, once you see Circle Line, Platform 6 and two five letter words as the blackboxed name. I wanted it to be a bonus &quot;haha, I know this&quot; moment, for literally anyone who takes the MRT here.</p>
<p>Why isn't this better contained? Who cares? It's a tiny horse with tiny people inside, rampaging on an ultramodern train station packed with commuters on <em>National Day, of all days</em>, while a disembodied voice obliviously warns commuters to Stand Behind The Yellow Line, Please Mind The Platform Gap, beepbeepbeepbeepbeepbeep. I could use the disused platform at Harbourfront though, mind posting its designation here? Like platform A or B or whatever.</p>
<p>(fun fact: 2965 is not a random number. I wrote this over the SG50 break. Best time to post the first scip located in the Finest City in the World, baby.)</p>

